{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1793569739,"nonce":"XZdT7cQUBjvEiZcLuwz90HOiDUE=","title":"cn::table body and footer text is near-black in dark mode","message":"Owner's dark-mode screenshot (cn_demo): body cells (INV001.., Paid, Credit Card, $250.00) and the footer row (Total, $1,980.00) draw near-black text on the dark surface. Headers and caption read fine.\n\nCause: `.cn-table-cell { }` is empty and nothing gives the table a `color`, so cell text falls back to the text default (black). Header and caption text are coloured in Rust with `ColorToken::TextSecondary` (table.rs), which also breaks the no-colour-in-Rust rule.\n\nashui (components.css 757-766):\n- table.ui-table { font-size: var(--text-sm) } (text inherits --text-primary from the page)\n- thead { background: var(--surface-overlay) }; tfoot { font-weight: 500; background: var(--surface-overlay) }\n- th.ui-table-head { min-height 40px; padding 0 16px; color: var(--text-secondary); font-weight 500 }\n- td.ui-table-cell { padding 12px 16px }\n- caption { color: var(--text-secondary) }\n- row hover color-mix(text-primary 4%), selected [data-state=\"selected\"] var(--selection), transition fast.\n\nDo: `.cn-table { color: var(--text-primary) }`, head/caption colour by rule, drop the Rust colours; selected row as `data-state=\"selected\"` (ties into 9375507, which wants it bindable). Check light and dark with recorder snapshots.","files":null}]}